The most recent version of the Mercedes-Benz CLK320 is the W209 model, produced from 2002 to 2005 before being replaced by the CLK350. There was also a CLK320 CDI diesel version available from 2005-2009. The user specified 'CLK320', which typically refers to the petrol model. Specs for the W209 CLK320 petrol include a 3.2L V6 engine producing 215 HP and 228 lb-ft of torque, paired with a 5-speed automatic transmission. It is rear-wheel drive. 0-60 mph is estimated around 6.9-7.9 seconds, and top speed is around 152 mph. Used prices are very low today. Reliability is generally considered good for the M112 V6 engine, but common issues include crankshaft position sensor failure, pixel loss in the instrument cluster, and potential rust. The W209 is based on the W203 C-Class platform. It's a 2-door coupe with 4 seats. Cargo space is around 15.4 cu ft. Dimensions are around 4.64m length, 1.74m width, and 1.41m height, with a wheelbase of 2.715m. Ground clearance is around 123-140mm (4.8-5.5 inches). Turning radius is around 10.7-10.8m (35.1-35.5 ft). Fuel economy is around 23-27 mpg combined, with CO2 emissions around 250 g/km. It lacks modern ADAS features and has a dated infotainment system with a small screen and no modern smartphone connectivity.

